#: src/lints.md:1
msgid "Lints"
msgstr ""

#: src/lints.md:3
msgid ""
"`rustdoc` provides lints to help you writing and testing your documentation. "
"You can use them like any other lints by doing this:"
msgstr ""

#: src/lints.md:7
msgid "// allows the lint, no diagnostics will be reported\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/lints.md:8
msgid "// warn if there are broken intra-doc links\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/lints.md:9
msgid "// error if there are broken intra-doc links\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/lints.md:12
msgid ""
"Note that, except for `missing_docs`, these lints are only available when "
"running `rustdoc`, not `rustc`."
msgstr ""

#: src/lints.md:14
msgid "Here is the list of the lints provided by `rustdoc`:"
msgstr ""

#: src/lints.md:16
msgid "`broken_intra_doc_links`"
msgstr ""

#: src/lints.md:18
msgid ""
"This lint **warns by default**. This lint detects when an [intra-doc link]"
"(write-documentation/linking-to-items-by-name.md) fails to be resolved. For "
"example:"
msgstr ""

#: src/lints.md:23
msgid "/// I want to link to [`Nonexistent`] but it doesn't exist!\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/lints.md:27
msgid "You'll get a warning saying:"
msgstr ""

#: src/lints.md:29
msgid ""
"```text\n"
"warning: unresolved link to `Nonexistent`\n"
" --> test.rs:1:24\n"
"  |\n"
"1 | /// I want to link to [`Nonexistent`] but it doesn't exist!\n"
"  |                        ^^^^^^^^^^^^^ no item named `Nonexistent` in "
"`test`\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/lints.md:37
msgid ""
"It will also warn when there is an ambiguity and suggest how to disambiguate:"
msgstr ""

#: src/lints.md:40
msgid "/// [`Foo`]\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/lints.md:48
msgid ""
"```text\n"
"warning: `Foo` is both an enum and a function\n"
" --> test.rs:1:6\n"
"  |\n"
"1 | /// [`Foo`]\n"
"  |      ^^^^^ ambiguous link\n"
"  |\n"
"  = note: `#[warn(rustdoc::broken_intra_doc_links)]` on by default\n"
"help: to link to the enum, prefix with the item type\n"
"  |\n"
"1 | /// [`enum@Foo`]\n"
"  |      ^^^^^^^^^^\n"
"help: to link to the function, add parentheses\n"
"  |\n"
"1 | /// [`Foo()`]\n"
"  |      ^^^^^^^\n"
"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/lints.md:67
msgid "`private_intra_doc_links`"
msgstr ""

#: src/lints.md:69
msgid ""
"This lint **warns by default**. This lint detects when [intra-doc links]"
"(write-documentation/linking-to-items-by-name.md) from public to private "
"items. For example:"
msgstr ""

#: src/lints.md:73 src/lints.md:242 src/lints.md:361 src/lints.md:433
msgid "// note: unnecessary - warns by default.\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/lints.md:74
msgid "/// [private]\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/lints.md:80
msgid ""
"This gives a warning that the link will be broken when it appears in your "
"documentation:"
msgstr ""

#: src/lints.md:82
msgid ""
"```text\n"
"warning: public documentation for `public` links to private item `private`\n"
" --> priv.rs:1:6\n"
"  |\n"
"1 | /// [private]\n"
"  |      ^^^^^^^ this item is private\n"
"  |\n"
"  = note: `#[warn(rustdoc::private_intra_doc_links)]` on by default\n"
"  = note: this link will resolve properly if you pass `--document-private-"
"items`\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/lints.md:93
msgid ""
"Note that this has different behavior depending on whether you pass `--"
"document-private-items` or not! If you document private items, then it will "
"still generate a link, despite the warning:"
msgstr ""

#: src/lints.md:96
msgid ""
"```text\n"
"warning: public documentation for `public` links to private item `private`\n"
" --> priv.rs:1:6\n"
"  |\n"
"1 | /// [private]\n"
"  |      ^^^^^^^ this item is private\n"
"  |\n"
"  = note: `#[warn(rustdoc::private_intra_doc_links)]` on by default\n"
"  = note: this link resolves only because you passed `--document-private-"
"items`, but will break without\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/lints.md:109
msgid "`missing_docs`"
msgstr ""

#: src/lints.md:111
msgid ""
"This lint is **allowed by default**. It detects items missing documentation. "
"For example:"
msgstr ""

#: src/lints.md:121
msgid "The `undocumented` function will then have the following warning:"
msgstr ""

#: src/lints.md:131
msgid ""
"Note that unlike other rustdoc lints, this lint is also available from "
"`rustc` directly."
msgstr ""

#: src/lints.md:133
msgid "`missing_crate_level_docs`"
msgstr ""

#: src/lints.md:135
msgid ""
"This lint is **allowed by default**. It detects if there is no documentation "
"at the crate root. For example:"
msgstr ""

#: src/lints.md:142
msgid "This will generate the following warning:"
msgstr ""

#: src/lints.md:144
msgid ""
"```text\n"
"warning: no documentation found for this crate's top-level module\n"
"  |\n"
"  = help: The following guide may be of use:\n"
"          https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/rustdoc/how-to-write-"
"documentation.html\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/lints.md:151
msgid ""
"This is currently \"allow\" by default, but it is intended to make this a "
"warning in the future. This is intended as a means to introduce new users on "
"_how_ to document their crate by pointing them to some instructions on how "
"to get started, without providing overwhelming warnings like `missing_docs` "
"might."
msgstr ""

#: src/lints.md:157
msgid "`missing_doc_code_examples`"
msgstr ""

#: src/lints.md:159
msgid ""
"This lint is **allowed by default** and is **nightly-only**. It detects when "
"a documentation block is missing a code example. For example:"
msgstr ""

#: src/lints.md:164
msgid "/// There is no code example!\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/lints.md:170
msgid "The `no_code_example` function will then have the following warning:"
msgstr ""

#: src/lints.md:172
msgid ""
"```text\n"
"warning: Missing code example in this documentation\n"
"  --> your-crate/lib.rs:3:1\n"
"   |\n"
"LL | /// There is no code example!\n"
"   | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/lints.md:180
msgid ""
"To fix the lint, you need to add a code example into the documentation block:"
msgstr ""

#: src/lints.md:183
msgid ""
"/// There is no code example!\n"
"///\n"
"/// ```\n"
"/// println!(\"calling no_code_example...\");\n"
"/// no_code_example();\n"
"/// println!(\"we called no_code_example!\");\n"
"/// ```\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/lints.md:193
msgid "This lint is not emitted on the following items:"
msgstr ""

#: src/lints.md:195
msgid "Impl blocks (both trait and inherent)"
msgstr ""

#: src/lints.md:196
msgid "Enum variants"
msgstr ""

#: src/lints.md:197
msgid "Struct/union fields"
msgstr ""

#: src/lints.md:198
msgid "Type aliases, including associated types"
msgstr ""

#: src/lints.md:199
msgid "Statics/constants"
msgstr ""

#: src/lints.md:200
msgid "Modules (including the top-level module of a crate)"
msgstr ""

#: src/lints.md:201
msgid "Foreign items from reexports (functions, statics, types, etc)"
msgstr ""

#: src/lints.md:203
msgid "`private_doc_tests`"
msgstr ""

#: src/lints.md:205
msgid ""
"This lint is **allowed by default**. It detects documentation tests when "
"they are on a private item. For example:"
msgstr ""

#: src/lints.md:212
msgid ""
"/// private doc test\n"
"    ///\n"
"    /// ```\n"
"    /// assert!(false);\n"
"    /// ```\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/lints.md:222 src/lints.md:252 src/lints.md:285 src/lints.md:330
#: src/lints.md:368 src/lints.md:400 src/lints.md:442
msgid "Which will give:"
msgstr ""

#: src/lints.md:224
msgid ""
"````text\n"
"warning: Documentation test in private item\n"
"  --> your-crate/lib.rs:4:1\n"
"   |\n"
" 4 | /     /// private doc test\n"
" 5 | |     ///\n"
" 6 | |     /// ```\n"
" 7 | |     /// assert!(false);\n"
" 8 | |     /// ```\n"
"   | |___________^\n"
"````"
msgstr ""

#: src/lints.md:236
msgid "`invalid_codeblock_attributes`"
msgstr ""

#: src/lints.md:238
msgid ""
"This lint **warns by default**. It detects code block attributes in "
"documentation examples that have potentially mis-typed values. For example:"
msgstr ""

#: src/lints.md:243
msgid ""
"/// Example.\n"
"///\n"
"/// ```should-panic\n"
"/// assert_eq!(1, 2);\n"
"/// ```\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/lints.md:254
msgid ""
"````text\n"
"warning: unknown attribute `should-panic`. Did you mean `should_panic`?\n"
" --> src/lib.rs:1:1\n"
"  |\n"
"1 | / /// Example.\n"
"2 | | ///\n"
"3 | | /// ```should-panic\n"
"4 | | /// assert_eq!(1, 2);\n"
"5 | | /// ```\n"
"  | |_______^\n"
"  |\n"
"  = note: `#[warn(rustdoc::invalid_codeblock_attributes)]` on by default\n"
"  = help: the code block will either not be tested if not marked as a rust "
"one or won't fail if it doesn't panic when running\n"
"````"
msgstr ""

#: src/lints.md:269
msgid ""
"In the example above, the correct form is `should_panic`. This helps detect "
"typo mistakes for some common attributes."
msgstr ""

#: src/lints.md:272
msgid "`invalid_html_tags`"
msgstr ""

#: src/lints.md:274
msgid ""
"This lint **warns by default**. It detects unclosed or invalid HTML tags. "
"For example:"
msgstr ""

#: src/lints.md:279
msgid ""
"/// <h1>\n"
"/// </script>\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/lints.md:287
msgid ""
"```text\n"
"warning: unopened HTML tag `script`\n"
" --> foo.rs:1:1\n"
"  |\n"
"1 | / /// <h1>\n"
"2 | | /// </script>\n"
"  | |_____________^\n"
"  |\n"
"  note: the lint level is defined here\n"
" --> foo.rs:1:9\n"
"  |\n"
"1 | #![warn(rustdoc::invalid_html_tags)]\n"
"  |         ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n"
"\n"
"warning: unclosed HTML tag `h1`\n"
" --> foo.rs:1:1\n"
"  |\n"
"1 | / /// <h1>\n"
"2 | | /// </script>\n"
"  | |_____________^\n"
"\n"
"warning: 2 warnings emitted\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/lints.md:311
msgid "`invalid_rust_codeblocks`"
msgstr ""

#: src/lints.md:313
msgid ""
"This lint **warns by default**. It detects Rust code blocks in documentation "
"examples that are invalid (e.g. empty, not parsable as Rust). For example:"
msgstr ""

#: src/lints.md:317
msgid ""
"/// Empty code blocks (with and without the `rust` marker):\n"
"///\n"
"/// ```rust\n"
"/// ```\n"
"///\n"
"/// Invalid syntax in code blocks:\n"
"///\n"
"/// ```rust\n"
"/// '<\n"
"/// ```\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/lints.md:332
msgid ""
"````text\n"
"warning: Rust code block is empty\n"
" --> lint.rs:3:5\n"
"  |\n"
"3 |   /// ```rust\n"
"  |  _____^\n"
"4 | | /// ```\n"
"  | |_______^\n"
"  |\n"
"  = note: `#[warn(rustdoc::invalid_rust_codeblocks)]` on by default\n"
"\n"
"warning: could not parse code block as Rust code\n"
"  --> lint.rs:8:5\n"
"   |\n"
"8  |   /// ```rust\n"
"   |  _____^\n"
"9  | | /// '<\n"
"10 | | /// ```\n"
"   | |_______^\n"
"   |\n"
"   = note: error from rustc: unterminated character literal\n"
"````"
msgstr ""

#: src/lints.md:355
msgid "`bare_urls`"
msgstr ""

#: src/lints.md:357
msgid ""
"This lint is **warn-by-default**. It detects URLs which are not links. For "
"example:"
msgstr ""

#: src/lints.md:362
msgid ""
"/// http://example.org\n"
"/// [http://example.net]\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/lints.md:370
msgid ""
"```text\n"
"warning: this URL is not a hyperlink\n"
" --> links.rs:1:5\n"
"  |\n"
"1 | /// http://example.org\n"
"  |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ help: use an automatic link instead: `<http://"
"example.org>`\n"
"  |\n"
"  = note: `#[warn(rustdoc::bare_urls)]` on by default\n"
"\n"
"warning: this URL is not a hyperlink\n"
" --> links.rs:3:6\n"
"  |\n"
"3 | /// [http://example.net]\n"
"  |      ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ help: use an automatic link instead: `<http://"
"example.net>`\n"
"\n"
"warning: 2 warnings emitted\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/lints.md:388
msgid "`unescaped_backticks`"
msgstr ""

#: src/lints.md:390
msgid ""
"This lint is **allowed by default**. It detects backticks (\\`) that are not "
"escaped. This usually means broken inline code. For example:"
msgstr ""

#: src/lints.md:395
msgid "/// `add(a, b) is the same as `add(b, a)`.\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/lints.md:402
msgid ""
"```text\n"
"warning: unescaped backtick\n"
" --> src/lib.rs:3:41\n"
"  |\n"
"3 | /// `add(a, b) is the same as `add(b, a)`.\n"
"  |                                         ^\n"
"  |\n"
"note: the lint level is defined here\n"
" --> src/lib.rs:1:9\n"
"  |\n"
"1 | #![warn(rustdoc::unescaped_backticks)]\n"
"  |         ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n"
"help: a previous inline code might be longer than expected\n"
"  |\n"
"3 | /// `add(a, b)` is the same as `add(b, a)`.\n"
"  |               +\n"
"help: if you meant to use a literal backtick, escape it\n"
"  |\n"
"3 | /// `add(a, b) is the same as `add(b, a)\\`.\n"
"  |                                         +\n"
"\n"
"warning: 1 warning emitted\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/lints.md:426
msgid "`redundant_explicit_links`"
msgstr ""

#: src/lints.md:428
msgid ""
"This lint is **warn-by-default**. It detects explicit links that are the "
"same as computed automatic links. This usually means the explicit links are "
"removable. For example:"
msgstr ""

#: src/lints.md:434
msgid ""
"/// add takes 2 [`usize`](usize) and performs addition\n"
"/// on them, then returns result.\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/lints.md:444
msgid ""
"```text\n"
"error: redundant explicit rustdoc link\n"
"  --> src/lib.rs:3:27\n"
"   |\n"
"3  | /// add takes 2 [`usize`](usize) and performs addition\n"
"   |                           ^^^^^\n"
"   |\n"
"   = note: Explicit link does not affect the original link\n"
"note: the lint level is defined here\n"
"  --> src/lib.rs:1:9\n"
"   |\n"
"1  | #![deny(rustdoc::redundant_explicit_links)]\n"
"   |         ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n"
"   = help: Remove explicit link instead\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
